nodes.body:
Thanks @0xtoward, this is really helpful! It's the same aliasing showing up in a sneakier way: the outputs stay identical, so you'd only notice the drop in acceptance. That lines up with the mechanism too. Anything that keeps a `read_accept` result around past the next replay ends up reading the next step's values.

Heads up that I rebased yesterday (now at `155fa07c`). On current main the in-graph accept writes its results through `out=`, so the PR now gives the writers a separate `accept_buffers(bs)` that returns views, and `read_accept` still hands out copies. If you have time to rerun your sync-loop MT-Bench check on the new head, I'd love to know it still gets you back to ~3.09.

@hnyls2002 @ch-wan this now covers two issues: the TP-rank deadlock in #42465 and this acceptance loss in the sync loop. Would one of you mind taking a look and adding `run-ci`?

